I don't have information that directly defines "syntax error" in the provided reference material. However, in C programming, a syntax error occurs when your code violates the specific grammatical rules and structure of the C language. It's akin to writing a sentence in English with incorrect grammar or punctuation; the compiler, which translates your C code into an executable program, cannot understand or process the instruction. These errors prevent your program from compiling successfully and must be corrected before the program can run. Common causes include missing semicolons, mismatched parentheses or braces, incorrect keywords, or improper variable declarations.

